[Room launch: the developer's network start uses the modules loaded at boot]
// Not a fix of the game and not in the fix set (sections-suggested.txt does not list it, so the
// set's figure is unchanged): the Mac application applies it by itself, beside the fix set, for
// the start of a room of our own (docs/issues/app-rendezvous.md). That start goes through the
// developer's branch of frontend_startNetGame, whose net_gameInit(0) calls net_loadModules
// 0x137a10 - written for a development kit: it loads every network module again although the
// retail boot (iop_loadModules 0x19ba98) has loaded them all, two of them from host0:, and reads
// the network setting from mc0:/BWCONFIG with the combination "Setting 1". On the emulator the
// second load of the modules brought the IOP down. Here the twelve module loads are left out and
// the setting is the retail one (mc0:/BWNETCNF/BWNETCNF, "Combination1", as the application
// writes it to the card); what the function then does - ezNetCnf, ezNetCtlInit, the interface
// up and the wait for it - is the game's own. net_loadModules is called from nowhere else, so a
// lobby game, an offline game and the native program are not touched.
patch=1,EE,00137A48,word,00000000
patch=1,EE,00137A94,word,00000000
patch=1,EE,00137AB4,word,00000000
patch=1,EE,00137AE4,word,00000000
patch=1,EE,00137B10,word,00000000
